      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>ADVANCE KNOWLEDGE OF BRAIN &amp; MENTAL HEALTH</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>WE MAINTAINED, CURATED AND PROVIDED UNRESTRICTED ACCESS TO A WEB-BASED DIGITAL MAP OF THE HUMAN BRAIN. THE DATA SERVER ALSO CONTAINS INFORMATION RELATIVE TO THE DONOR'S MEDICAL CASE, THAT OF THE AMNESIC PATIENT HM WHICH IS THE MOST INFLUENTIAL CASES IN THE HISTORY OF NEUROSCIENCE.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>175246</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>THE ORGANIZATION CONTINUES TO OCCUPY A SPACE IN DOWNTOWN SAN DIEGO, CA AS THE PRIMARY SITE FOR OPERATIONS AND PROGRAMS. WE CONTINUE TO LEASE A 4,000 SQUARE FOOT GALLERY SPACE THAT WAS RE-PURPOSED AS A EXHIBITION SPACE FOR NEUROSCIENCE AND NEUROTECHNOLOGY. THE VENUE HOUSES A BRAIN IMAGING LABORTORY EQUIPPED WITH RESEARCH-GRADE SCIENTIFIC INSTRUMENTATION. THE LABORATORY WILL SERVE THE DUAL PURPOSES OF ADVANCING RESEARCH ON NEURODEGENERATIVE DISEASES LIKE ALZHEIMER'S AND PARKINSON'S WHILE ALSO SERVING AS A TEACHING LAB FOR STUDENTS. CREATING SUCH A NOVEL SPACE FULLFILLS ONE OF OUR PRIMARY GOALS WHICH IS TO MAKE BIOMEDICAL RESEARCH MORE RELIABLE AND TRANSPARENT TO PUBLIC SCRUTINY AND PROVIDE ACCESS TO SCIENCE EDUCATION TO AT-RISK YOUTH FROM DISADVANTAGED BACKGROUNDS - HENCE OUR CENTRAL LOCATION. OTHER EXPENSES (FORM 990Z LINE 16) RELATES PRIMARILY TO CONSTURCTION COSTS AS WELL AS SUPPLIES AND EQUIPMENT RELATIVE TO FURNISHING THE VENUE AND BUILDING THE LABORATORY, INCLUDING WEB ACCESSIBILITY, ETC.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>We completed construction and opened operations of a brain museum in downtown San Diego. The museum hosts a unique colleciton of donated human brains and houese a fully-functional brain imaging laboratory that has been re-designed to support science education programs in collaboration with local school districts.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
